{title: The Day of Resurrection}
{artist: John of Damascus; tr. John Mason Neale}
{genre: Easter}
{style: Hymn}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]The day of resur[D]rection
[G]Earth, tell it out a[D]broad
[G]The Passover of [C]gladness
[G]The Passover of [D]God[G]
[G]From death to life e[D]ternal
[G]From earth unto the [D]sky
[G]Our Christ hath brought us [C]over
[G]With hymns of vic[D]tory[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Our hearts be pure from [D]evil
[G]That we may see a[D]right
[G]The Lord in rays e[C]ternal
[G]Of resurrection [D]light[G]
[G]And listening to His [D]accents
[G]May hear, so calm and [D]plain
[G]His own All hail, and [C]hearing
[G]May raise the victor [D]strain[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Now let the heavens be [D]joyful
[G]Let earth her song be[D]gin
[G]Let the round world keep [C]triumph
[G]And all that is there[D]in[G]
[G]Invisible and [D]visible
[G]Their notes let all things [D]blend
[G]For Christ the Lord is [C]risen
[G]Our joy that hath no [D]end[G]
{end_of_verse}
